WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.884
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:06.184 --> 00:00:09.664
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.964 --> 00:00:15.774
Unit twenty-eight: Quantifying Expressions. Today you will state amounts precisely and formally.

4
00:00:16.074 --> 00:00:18.540
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.756
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:24.838
A great deal of.

7
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:29.161
A great deal of means a large amount of something uncountable.

8
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.215
A great deal of money.

9
00:00:31.817 --> 00:00:34.899
Your turn. Say: A great deal of.

10
00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:39.048
A great deal of.

11
00:00:39.783 --> 00:00:41.156
A handful of.

12
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.649
A handful of means a very small number.

13
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.110
A handful of students came.

14
00:00:47.717 --> 00:00:50.404
Your turn. Say: A handful of.

15
00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.558
A handful of.

16
00:00:55.317 --> 00:00:56.701
The vast majority of.

17
00:00:57.717 --> 00:01:00.041
The vast majority of means almost all.

18
00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.812
The vast majority of people agree.

19
00:01:03.417 --> 00:01:06.800
Your turn. Say: The vast majority of.

20
00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.399
The vast majority of.

21
00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.523
A fair amount of.

22
00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:17.387
A fair amount of means a reasonable quantity.

23
00:01:17.983 --> 00:01:19.507
A fair amount of work.

24
00:01:20.117 --> 00:01:22.769
Your turn. Say: A fair amount of.

25
00:01:25.633 --> 00:01:26.855
A fair amount of.

26
00:01:27.617 --> 00:01:28.862
Scarcely any.

27
00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:31.850
Scarcely any means almost none.

28
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.113
There was scarcely any time.

29
00:01:34.717 --> 00:01:37.520
Your turn. Say: Scarcely any.

30
00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:41.658
Scarcely any.

31
00:01:42.417 --> 00:01:43.499
A wealth of.

32
00:01:44.483 --> 00:01:47.400
A wealth of means a large amount of valuable things.

33
00:01:48.017 --> 00:01:49.656
A wealth of information.

34
00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:53.065
Your turn. Say: A wealth of.

35
00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:56.866
A wealth of.

36
00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:58.711
A host of.

37
00:01:59.717 --> 00:02:01.867
A host of means a large number of.

38
00:02:02.483 --> 00:02:03.926
A host of problems.

39
00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:07.297
Your turn. Say: A host of.

40
00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:11.309
A host of.

41
00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:13.237
Approximately.

42
00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.865
Approximately means about, not exact.

43
00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.322
Approximately ten people.

44
00:02:19.917 --> 00:02:22.627
Your turn. Say: Approximately.

45
00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:26.700
Approximately.

46
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.476
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:32.317 --> 00:02:37.416
Visal, why is the vast majority of people agree better than many people agree in an essay?

48
00:02:38.517 --> 00:02:50.573
It is more precise. Quantifying expressions tell the reader how much or how many: a handful means very few, the vast majority means nearly all.

49
00:02:51.683 --> 00:02:53.834
Which go with uncountable nouns?

50
00:02:54.950 --> 00:03:09.503
A great deal of, a fair amount of and a wealth of go with uncountable nouns: a great deal of money, a wealth of information. A handful of, a host of and a number of go with plural countable nouns.

51
00:03:10.617 --> 00:03:12.268
What about verb agreement?

52
00:03:13.383 --> 00:03:27.602
The vast majority of students are happy takes a plural verb because of the noun. But a number of takes a plural verb, while the number of takes a singular verb. Approximately adds a hedge before a number.

53
00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.186
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:37.380
Grammar focus: Quantifiers: quantifying phrase plus of plus noun; agreement follows the noun.

55
00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:38.855
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:42.049
A great deal of money was spent on the project.

57
00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.774
The vast majority of students are satisfied.

58
00:03:46.683 --> 00:03:49.670
A wealth of information is available online.

59
00:03:50.633 --> 00:03:59.091
Use a great deal of and a wealth of with uncountable nouns, and a handful of, a host of and the vast majority of with plurals. The verb agrees with the noun.

60
00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:03.663
Be careful! Don't say: A great deal of students came.

61
00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.598
Say: A great number of students came.

62
00:04:08.898 --> 00:04:10.689
Match with countable nouns.

63
00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:14.303
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.484
How Much, How Many?.

65
00:04:16.784 --> 00:04:19.550
A great deal of money was spent on the new library.

66
00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:23.321
The vast majority of students use it every week.

67
00:04:24.333 --> 00:04:26.902
Only a handful of them complained about the noise.

68
00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.817
The library offers a wealth of information online.

69
00:04:31.833 --> 00:04:34.564
Precise quantifiers make a report more convincing.

70
00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:40.040
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:40.883 --> 00:04:44.197
blank of students are satisfied. (almost all)

72
00:04:44.497 --> 00:04:48.929
A, The vast majority. B, A handful. C, Scarcely any.

73
00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:55.105
The answer is A: The vast majority.

74
00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.215
A great deal of blank was spent.

75
00:04:58.515 --> 00:05:02.110
A, students. B, money. C, coins.

76
00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.353
The answer is B: money.

77
00:05:08.517 --> 00:05:10.040
A handful of means blank.

78
00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:14.098
A, very few. B, nearly all. C, half.

79
00:05:17.633 --> 00:05:19.993
The answer is A: very few.

80
00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.929
Scarcely any means blank.

81
00:05:23.229 --> 00:05:26.488
A, some. B, almost none. C, a lot.

82
00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:32.323
The answer is B: almost none.

83
00:05:33.483 --> 00:05:36.586
According to the reading, what does the library offer?

84
00:05:36.886 --> 00:05:42.501
A, a wealth of information. B, a handful of seats. C, scarcely any books.

85
00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:49.053
The answer is A: a wealth of information.

86
00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:53.302
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:57.996
Rewrite 'Many people agree' using a more precise quantifying expression.

88
00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:08.307
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:08.607 --> 00:06:20.225
The vast majority of people agree. Approximately eighty percent of the people I asked agreed. These expressions are more precise, so they make my claim stronger.

90
00:06:20.525 --> 00:06:22.408
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:23.317 --> 00:06:31.170
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and quantifiers: quantifying phrase plus of plus noun; agreement follows the noun.

92
00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:36.712
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

93
00:06:37.012 --> 00:06:39.664
See you in Unit twenty-nine. Goodbye!

94
00:06:39.964 --> 00:06:42.605
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

